<title>CHINA: Far East Hotels year net returns to gain.</title>
<headline>Far East Hotels year net returns to gain.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 0.9 gain    vs 0.4 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  nil	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	3.81 loss   vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			  4.13 profit vs 1.81 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		   67.50	 vs 65.51</p>
<p>    Company name	     Far East Hotels and Entertainment Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		September 22-26</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Far East Hotels operates hotels, cinemas, amusement parks and bowling centres.</p>
<p>Upon the closure of Lai Chi Kok Amusenemt Park and Sung Dynasty Village on April 1, 1997, the operation results for the year together with comparative figures have been reflected as discontinued operation.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on disposal of fixed assets of HK$1.40 million and provision for long service payment of HK$2.42 million.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
